From 109631bdce64aa306a025c0d7536b0c4be0c4aa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Virgile-pct <pourchetvirgile@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:42:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] skippy: record per-token logprobs while sampling

A sampling config with SKIPPY_SAMPLING_FLAG_LOGPROBS records, for every
token skippy_sample_token_ith samples, the token's log-probability under the
raw distribution (temperature 1, before penalties or truncation) and its
top_logprobs most likely alternatives (at most SKIPPY_MAX_TOP_LOGPROBS, 20).
skippy_session_take_token_logprobs moves them out, oldest first; a session
reset drops them. A logprobs request never attaches backend (in-graph)
sampling, which skips copying the raw logits row; a token drawn while the
lane still carried a backend sampler from an earlier request is recorded
as unreadable instead of being read from a stale row. ABI 0.1.72 -> 0.1.73.
